<GuideLayout slug="gear-upgrades" updated="2026-11-21">
  <h2>The auction house is full of upgrades</h2>
  <p>While you level, your gear falls behind quickly, and quest rewards don't fill every slot. Meanwhile other players list hundreds of green and blue items, many of them for less than a few minutes of questing earns. The hard part is finding the ones that fit your character among thousands of listings. The <a href="/upgrades">Gear upgrades</a> page does that search for you.</p>

  <h2>Step 1: look up your character</h2>
  <p>Type your character's name. In WoW: Forever that's the full name, first name and last name, spelled exactly as in game. We ask Blizzard for your public profile and read what you're wearing in every slot.</p>
  <p class="tip">Blizzard updates profiles after you <b>log out</b>. If you just equipped something new and it doesn't show, log out to the character screen and look up the name again a few minutes later.</p>

  <h2>Step 2: what counts as an upgrade</h2>
  <p>We then check every weapon and armor piece listed on the auction houses you can buy from: your faction's and Blackwater. An item is shown as an upgrade only when all of these are true:</p>
  <ul class="gems">
    <li>Its <b>item level</b> is higher than what you wear in that slot. The <b>Better by</b> column shows by how much.</li>
    <li>Your <b>class can use it</b>: the right armor type (cloth, leather, mail or plate, including mail and plate from level 40 for the classes that learn them) and the right weapon types.</li>
    <li>You're <b>high enough level</b> to equip it.</li>
    <li>For rings and trinkets, it beats the <b>weaker</b> of the two you wear.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Step 3: check the stats</h2>
  <p>Item level is the one thing we know for every item, so the list is a shortlist, not a verdict. A higher item level with the wrong stats can be worse for you: a caster gains little from a strength ring. Hover any item to see its full tooltip and compare it with what you wear before you buy.</p>
  <p>Use <b>Price per item</b> to hide anything above your budget. Prices are the cheapest listing on each house, refreshed about every hour, and the table shows which house it's on.</p>

  <h2>Getting the most from it</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Check every few levels: each level unlocks items you couldn't wear before.</li>
    <li>Start with slots where <b>Better by</b> is largest. A big jump in one slot is usually worth more than small ones everywhere.</li>
    <li>Weapons first for melee and hunters; their damage matters more than any armor slot.</li>
    <li>Remember that green items with random enchantments ("of the Bear", "of the Eagle") share an item level but not stats: read the tooltip.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>The character page</h2>
  <p>The same lookup works on the <a href="/character">Character lookup</a> page, which shows the whole character: equipped gear with average item level, professions with their skill, and top reputations. Use <b>Copy link</b> to share it with your guild. Profiles are fetched live from Blizzard and cached for at most 15 minutes. We don't keep them, and you can ask us to hide a character; see the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p>
</GuideLayout>
